  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two reactions are given below:<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Δ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>822</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Δ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>110</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Then enthalpy change for following reaction<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "492",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Enthalpy change is the standard enthalpy of formation, in any general chemical reaction, the reactants undergo chemical changes and combine to give products. It can be represented by the following equation:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Reactant</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Product</mi></math></p><p>From the given equations,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Δ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>822</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> .........(i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ΔH</mi><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>110</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>....(ii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ΔH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>?</mo></math></p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ΔH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> can be calculated as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ΔH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>ΔH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>ΔH</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>110</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>822</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>492</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mole</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
